\`\`\`csharp
MessageTokensCount result = await client.Messages.CountTokens(new MessageCountTokensParams {
    Model = Model.ClaudeOpus4_6,
    Messages = [new() { Role = Role.User, Content = "Hello" }],
});
long tokens = result.InputTokens;
\`\`\`

\`MessageCountTokensParams.Tools\` uses a different union type (\`MessageCountTokensTool\`) than \`MessageCreateParams.Tools\` (\`ToolUnion\`) \u2014 if you're passing tools, the compiler will tell you when it matters.

